  "annotation": "Spring 2026 is the semester to examine: enrollment barely moved and <strong>retention rose to 91%</strong>, but attendance <strong>fell from 90% to 65%</strong>.",
  "insight": "The three metrics can disagree, and which one dips tells you what is wrong. Students are still <em>signing up and staying signed up</em> -- retention is the best it has been -- but they are not <em>turning up</em>. That is an attendance problem, not a retention problem, and the fixes are different: a scheduling or session-quality issue rather than a recruitment one. Retention alone would have said the club was healthier than ever."
